export anchor BauhausStyle:
    number: 18
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Bauhaus
    idea: Primary red, yellow and blue blocks locked together by thick black bars, with circles, squares and triangles as both structure and status.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #f5f1e8, the page
        white: #ffffff, fields, the chart box and the style sheet
        black: #111111, text, the header, thick bars, progress fills and the hours block
        red: #d1281f, the primary button, the overdue block, the Behind square and this week's bars
        redText: #b8211a, red text on paper when needed
        yellow: #f2c230, the date tag, the activity panel, the tasks due block and the At risk triangle
        blue: #1f4fa0, the focus outline, the active projects block, the On track circle and last week's bars
        track: #d9d4c7, the empty part of progress bars
        cream: #fff8dc, a focused field and a focused row
    type:
        Geometric sans, Futura, Futura PT, Century Gothic, Avenir Next,
        Avenir, Trebuchet MS, Gill Sans, sans-serif. Summary figures are
        80px extra bold with tight tracking, the greeting 64px extra bold
        capitals, section titles 28px extra bold capitals, project names
        18px extra bold in sentence case, body 16px medium, and labels 13
        to 14px extra bold capitals with 0.08em tracking.
    layout:
        A black header with a 12px red bar under it holds a red square logo
        with a yellow circle, the capital wordmark, capital nav links with
        a 4px yellow underline on Home, a search field with a yellow square
        icon cell, a red New project button, a blue square showing the
        notification count and a yellow initials circle. The hero is a
        seven to five split, a yellow date tag, the huge greeting and a
        white strip with a thick red left edge saying 4 tasks are overdue
        on the left, and a composition of a blue circle, a yellow square, a
        red triangle, an open black ring and crossing black bars on the
        right. A 12px black bar tops four unequal summary blocks in blue,
        yellow, red and black. Below, a seven to five split puts the
        projects list on the left and a white chart box with a yellow
        corner square above a yellow activity panel on the right. Below
        900px the splits stack and the summary goes two by two, and below
        560px the project rows stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px block padding, 32 to 56px between bands and a 40px column gap.
    density: Bold and medium. Few, large elements in an uneven grid.
    corners: None. Only true circles are round.
    borders: Thick black bars, 12px under the header and above the summary, 8px above each section title, 4px around boxes, fields and secondary buttons and 2px between rows.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from flat overlapping colour.
    icons:
        Solid geometric glyphs only. Status is a blue circle for On track,
        a yellow triangle with a black outline for At risk and a red square
        for Behind, always beside the capital word, and a key under the
        list spells this out. Summary labels and activity bullets use solid
        white or black circles, squares, triangles and a quarter circle.
        Progress is a 14px black bar on the track colour.
    focus: A 4px blue outline offset 3px. Controls on the black header use a 4px yellow outline, and a focused field also takes the cream fill.
    tone: Direct and declarative with capital labels, such as Good afternoon, Mara. and 4 tasks are overdue.
